{
  "path": "/configuration/environment/",
  "title": "Environment reference | My Claude Code",
  "description": "The variable names My Claude Code reads, grouped by area, with what each one decides. Names and purposes only: no values, and no sample secrets.",
  "nav": "Environment",
  "eyebrow": "Configuration · Environment",
  "h1": "Environment reference",
  "intro": "This page is the LLM gateway environment variables reference. It names the settings, grouped by what they decide, and gives no values. For a secret-like variable it never shows an example: a documentation page is not a place to invent one. The annotated .env.example carries the same names, with comments.",
  "page_grid": true,
  "breadcrumbs": [
    {
      "label": "Home",
      "href": "/"
    },
    {
      "label": "Configuration",
      "href": "/configuration/"
    },
    {
      "label": "Environment"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "text": "<strong>Names, not values.</strong> Nothing on this page is a usable setting. Copy a name into your own .env and read its comment in <code>.env.example</code> before choosing a value."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Core server"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "Name",
        "What it decides"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "<code>HOST</code>",
          "the address the server listens on; loopback by default"
        ],
        [
          "<code>PORT</code>",
          "the port the server listens on; 8082 by default"
        ],
        [
          "<code>ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN</code>",
          "the bearer token proxy clients present; generated for this machine on first start; required once the host is not loopback"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MCC_CONFIG_DIR</code>",
          "the configuration home; environment-only, resolved before the .env is read"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MCC_ENV_FILE</code>",
          "an explicit dotenv file to load instead of the default one"
        ],
        [
          "<code>LOG_LEVEL</code>",
          "the server log level"
        ],
        [
          "<code>SERVER_LOG_RETAIN_FILES</code>",
          "how many rotated server log files are kept"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Request log and analytics"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "Name",
        "What it decides"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "<code>REQUEST_LOG_ENABLED</code>",
          "whether the persistent request log, and therefore Analytics, is on"
        ],
        [
          "<code>REQUEST_LOG_MAX_ROWS</code>",
          "the retention cap; the oldest rows are pruned periodically"
        ],
        [
          "<code>LOG_RAW_API_PAYLOADS</code>",
          "whether API payloads are kept raw"
        ],
        [
          "<code>LOG_RAW_SSE_EVENTS</code>",
          "whether streamed events are kept raw"
        ],
        [
          "<code>LOG_RAW_UPSTREAM_BYTES</code>",
          "whether the provider's own bytes are kept exactly as received; off by default"
        ],
        [
          "<code>LOG_API_ERROR_TRACEBACKS</code>",
          "whether API error tracebacks are kept"
        ],
        [
          "<code>LOG_RAW_CLI_DIAGNOSTICS</code>",
          "whether CLI diagnostics are kept raw"
        ],
        [
          "<code>USAGE_AUTO_REFRESH_SECONDS</code>",
          "how often the Usage page refreshes itself while open; zero turns it off"
        ],
        [
          "<code>USAGE_LAYOUT</code>",
          "which of the five Usage layouts is shown"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Models, tiers and reasoning"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "Name",
        "What it decides"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "<code>MODEL</code>",
          "the model used when nothing more specific matches"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MODEL_MYTHOS</code>, <code>MODEL_FABLE</code>, <code>MODEL_OPUS</code>, <code>MODEL_SONNET</code>, <code>MODEL_HAIKU</code>",
          "each coding-agent tier's model"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MODEL_VISION</code>",
          "the model the vision adapter routes an image request to"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MODEL_*_FALLBACKS</code>",
          "each route's ordered stand-ins"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MODEL_*_PAUSED</code>",
          "the entries kept in place but never tried"
        ],
        [
          "<code>HARNESS_TIER_ALIASES</code>",
          "whether the per-agent tier aliases are offered"
        ],
        [
          "<code>VISION_ADAPTER_MODE</code>",
          "route, describe or the behaviour the request would have had without the adapter"
        ],
        [
          "<code>REASONING_POLICY</code>",
          "the root reasoning policy"
        ],
        [
          "<code>REASONING_MYTHOS</code>, <code>REASONING_FABLE</code>, <code>REASONING_OPUS</code>, <code>REASONING_SONNET</code>, <code>REASONING_HAIKU</code>",
          "per-tier reasoning overrides"
        ],
        [
          "<code>REASONING_EFFORT_BUDGET_RATIOS</code>",
          "how much of the output allowance a thinking rung may take"
        ],
        [
          "<code>REASONING_ANSWER_FLOOR_MAX</code>",
          "the answer reserve kept aside from the thinking budget"
        ],
        [
          "<code>PROMPT_CACHE_TTL</code>, <code>PROMPT_CACHE_TTL_*</code>",
          "the prompt-cache lifetime per route or per tier; client by default"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Output budgets, retries and limits"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "Name",
        "What it decides"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "<code>MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS_CEILING</code>",
          "the ceiling applied to an output budget; zero is the sentinel for none"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS_FLOOR</code>",
          "the floor that stops a long prompt squeezing the reply to nothing"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS_UNKNOWN_DEFAULT</code>",
          "the value used when no source publishes a model's limit"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS_CONTEXT_MARGIN</code>, <code>MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS_CONTEXT_FLOOR</code>",
          "the context-headroom bounds"
        ],
        [
          "<code>FALLBACK_TOTAL_TIMEOUT</code>, <code>FALLBACK_FIRST_TOKEN_TIMEOUT</code>, <code>FALLBACK_STALL_TIMEOUT</code>",
          "the deadlines that make a silent model a failure"
        ],
        [
          "<code>FALLBACK_RETRY_FIRST</code>, <code>FALLBACK_SKIP_KINDS</code>",
          "what the chain retries and what it skips"
        ],
        [
          "<code>FALLBACK_BENCH_ENABLED</code>, <code>FALLBACK_EJECT_*</code>",
          "whether and when a chain entry is benched"
        ],
        [
          "<code>PROVIDER_RETRY_ATTEMPTS</code>, <code>PROVIDER_RETRY_BACKOFF_*</code>",
          "the retry count and backoff"
        ],
        [
          "<code>RATE_LIMIT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS</code>, <code>RATE_LIMIT_COOLDOWN_MAX_SECONDS</code>, <code>RATE_LIMIT_COOLDOWN_MODE</code>",
          "what a 429 costs a key"
        ],
        [
          "<code>RATE_LIMIT_ROUTES_AROUND_MODEL</code>",
          "whether a 429 tries another model on the same provider"
        ],
        [
          "<code>CREDENTIAL_LOCKOUT_TIERS</code>",
          "the escalating bench for a rejected key"
        ],
        [
          "<code>CREDENTIAL_MODEL_BENCH_ESCALATION</code>",
          "how many models must be limited before the whole key is benched"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Web search and fetch"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "Name",
        "What it decides"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "<code>WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER</code>",
          "auto, off, disabled or one search backend"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEB_SEARCH_FALLBACK_POLICY</code>",
          "how far the search chain may move"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEB_SEARCH_CHAIN</code>, <code>WEB_SEARCH_CHAIN_PAUSED</code>",
          "the ordered search services and the ones paused"
        ],
        [
          "<code>ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS</code>",
          "whether web search and web fetch are fulfilled at the proxy"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEBSEARCH_PROXY</code>",
          "an optional outbound proxy for search"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEBSEARCH_LEGACY_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS</code>",
          "optional spacing between keyless-hop requests"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEBSEARCH_LOG_ENABLED</code>, <code>WEBSEARCH_LOG_MAX_ROWS</code>",
          "the web-search log and its retention"
        ],
        [
          "<code>DDGS_REGION</code>, <code>DDGS_TIMELIMIT</code>, <code>DDGS_BACKEND</code>, <code>DDGS_SAFESEARCH</code>",
          "the keyless metasearch's region, freshness, engine and safe-search"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEB_FETCH_EXTRACTOR</code>",
          "the page extractor; basic restores earlier bytes"
        ],
        [
          "<code>WEB_FETCH_ALLOWED_SCHEMES</code>, <code>WEB_FETCH_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORKS</code>",
          "the web-fetch egress rules"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Media, messaging and the dashboard"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "Name",
        "What it decides"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "<code>MODEL_IMAGE</code>, <code>MODEL_TTS</code>, <code>MODEL_ASR</code>, <code>MODEL_VIDEO</code>",
          "the four media rails and their chains"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MEDIA_UPLOAD_MAX_MB</code>",
          "the optional media upload cap"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MEDIA_STORE_ENABLED</code>, <code>MEDIA_STORE_MAX_MB</code>",
          "whether generated media is stored, and its size cap"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MCP_MEDIA_APPS</code>",
          "the agents the media server is added to"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MESSAGING_PLATFORM</code>",
          "discord, telegram or none"
        ],
        [
          "<code>MESSAGING_RATE_LIMIT</code>, <code>MESSAGING_RATE_WINDOW</code>",
          "the outbound message rate"
        ],
        [
          "<code>ADMIN_DESIGN</code>, <code>ADMIN_THEME</code>, <code>ADMIN_MODE</code>, <code>ADMIN_DENSITY</code>",
          "the dashboard's machine-wide appearance"
        ],
        [
          "<code>ENABLE_TITLE_GENERATION_SKIP</code>, <code>ENABLE_SUGGESTION_MODE_SKIP</code>",
          "the local optimization rules"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Reading a name"
    },
    {
      "type": "ul",
      "items": [
        "A blank value means unset; the default applies.",
        "A restart-required setting is labelled on the dashboard, because the running process read it at startup.",
        "A value is never published here, and a secret-like name never gets an example."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "related",
      "links": [
